			"Message": "build(SideCar): Add Git LFS support for Node.js binaries and version cache\n\nThis commit introduces Git LFS tracking for Node.js binaries across multiple platforms (aarch64, x86_64) in the SideCar repository. New directory structures with .gitkeep files ensure proper version segregation, while Cache.json maintains version mappings for cross-platform compatibility.\n\nThe changes to .gitattributes add LFS filters for all Node.js executables and tools (node, npm, npx, corepack) in platform-specific directories. The updated .gitignore rules prevent accidental binary commits outside designated paths while preserving .gitkeep files for empty directory tracking. The Cache.json file establishes a version registry that will be used by Mountain's build.rs script to select appropriate runtimes during sidecar initialization.\n\nThis setup optimizes binary storage efficiency via LFS and provides a centralized reference for Node.js runtime versions used in the Tauri-based Mountain backend's sidecar management.",
			"SHA": "5992828569e3e6b0b755c32a589de33e24d30231"
		},
