		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2025-06-30T12:47:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				323,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(SideCar): Replace custom logging with standard `log` crate\n\nThis commit transitions the SideCar download utility from custom logging functions to the standardized `log` crate macros (`info!`, `warn!`, `error!`), aligning with Land's broader architectural principles:\n\n1. **Why:** Custom logging functions were replaced to leverage Rust's ecosystem standards, enabling better integration with Land's centralized logging infrastructure planned for `Mountain`. This supports future cross-component log aggregation and level filtering via the `RUST_LOG` environment variable.\n\n2. **What:**\n   - Removed all custom `LogInfo`/`LogWarn`/etc. functions\n   - Replaced 25+ log calls with equivalent `log` macros\n   - Updated `Logger()` configuration to colorize \"Download\" tag as cyan\n   - Enhanced `main()` error handling to log fatal errors before exit\n\n3. **Impact:**\n   - Standardizes logging across Land's Rust components\n   - Prepares for unified log management in `Mountain`\n   - Maintains identical console output while improving maintainability\n   - Fixes potential log duplication issues in the download workflow\n\nRefs #logging-standardization",
			"SHA": "88cd9893c708258fa207fd253d50b60bd72594f3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2025-06-30T12:45:22Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				323,
				18
			],
			"Message": "feat(SideCar): Initialize project with CI/CD, config, and download logic\n\nAdded comprehensive project setup for the SideCar component, which handles dependency management for the Land editor ecosystem. Key changes include:\n- Implemented GitHub workflows for automated builds (Rust.yml), dependency updates (Dependabot.yml), issue assignment (GitHub.yml), and daily updates (Auto.yml)\n- Configured Cargo build settings for optimized release builds\n- Added project documentation (README, CONTRIBUTING, CODE_OF_CONDUCT, SECURITY) and licensing\n- Implemented core download functionality in Rust with:\n  - Concurrent downloads using Tokio\n  - Caching mechanism\n  - Structured logging\n  - Node.js version resolution\n\nThis establishes the foundation for SideCar's role in managing dependencies (like Node.js for Cocoon) in Land's architecture, supporting MVP Path A's extension ecosystem. The download service will be integrated with Mountain to provide required runtimes for the Cocoon sidecar.",
			"SHA": "5e69f755ef9238b5d0789a5738e659ade3fc59c6"
		},
