			],
			"Message": "docs(Build): Add README for SideCar runtime directory\n\nAdded comprehensive documentation for the SideCar directory which stores pre-compiled native dependencies required by the Land ecosystem. This directory is critical for MVP Path A implementation where we bundle Node.js for the Cocoon extension host to ensure portability without requiring pre-installed runtimes.\n\nThe README explains:\n1. Purpose of vendoring runtimes like Node.js for Cocoon\n2. Directory structure organized by target-triple (e.g., x86_64-pc-windows-msvc)\n3. Integration with Mountain's build system via Build.rs\n4. Usage of Download.sh for populating binaries\n5. Important note about excluding binaries from version control\n\nThis documentation aligns with Land's architecture by clarifying how we maintain the self-contained nature of the application while leveraging external runtimes, directly supporting the Cocoon sidecar implementation strategy.",
